      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TEDDY DANGER (1) had been racing in honest fashion recording two placings in a row before finishing fifth (19.74) at this track latest. Solid record here at the distance winning two races. Goes very well from this draw with six wins and three minor placings from 10 starts. Can discover winning form. BUNDABERG GUM (2) was responsible for a modest effort most recently when eighth at this track over 340m behind Very Sneaky (20.65) in a Other. Likely to be thereabouts. STRANGER DANGER (3) doesn't have the best strike-rate. Finished third (30.76) at Launceston latest and might be close to finding winning form again. Yet to win out of this box but has been in the placings four times from seven starts. Leading player again. WORPEL (7) missed the placings here last start but is well-placed to make amends.",
